 "name": "wolverine_skull",
 "description": "Side view of a wolverine skull, facing right (041 s034/s035, pairs with dog_skull at the same overall size): cream #efe2c0 bone with grey-tan spray shading. Short, heavy and wide: a tall sagittal crest hooking back over the occiput, short blunt muzzle, small orbit opening into a deep dark temporal fossa that holds a huge coronoid process, a thick bowed zygomatic arch, a MASSIVE deep lower jaw (slightly parted), and big teeth: long upper and lower canines, a huge notched upper carnassial. Clean bone, no gore. Anchor centre, about 470x300 (x -236..234, y -142..158).",
